<description>&lt;p&gt;US authorities have taken a fugitive businessman into custody in Venezuela on bribery charges while Maduro appears in court as the United States targets his associates in a corruption scandal and a judge denied medical bail for Cilia Flores, prompting solidarity campaigns. An aid worker reports severe earthquake damage in Venezuela and Starlink internet is now permitted to operate in the country, while Cuba’s grid collapse adds regional energy strain. Energy firms are recruiting former US officials to access Venezuelan oil and allegations claim a PDVSA plane was used to transport goods. The UCDP counted 2 battle-related deaths in 2007.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxOX0dPTzMxQmZlR2ROS0E2T3czWFg4ZVNHb1A3NG9fdmFsQzdhSG5YOTBMVHgxZzEyeTJpaWZYMHNuaW52WlZmNHItb1hmR2xha1ZtemVjSkw4U2psUzdNRVFGTmFUQXVJRmJudGVPMzFSRnFtSUhrQ1F3b3lvTERwVjI1VkkzUXZnaUo5U2Z3ZWRxNnl4S1ppRFJ6RlJ3WkZUNFpjZkM2OUw0NnV4MG5yUVQ1Zms0N25od1NySEZIUERMMjg?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxNOGg5cUFTeG5wT2g5bzdaWGowSDFILV85S0RhMnhUQmRpMG1lMkc5TDI3V1cwNUlvMnBRQ2ZyQUZOYVNnRnRNWmdqVFZFUUhBZThMSElNR0RVZDRRS1gwY1VVeldSWlE2cktqazFzQVFGWUJrZnlYVGppd1dxYlpyV2p1NU5xa3ZGYTVWXzlBNUdtVDhFdEJkaW5n?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxOY2dqa3hDUGJObnZUWGtlc1dKaUpFazdkSW9HYko3eGU2SmZJS2pRR1luT2RlWFBEZkpqWmJ1V1lzdFB0RUNHTHpmRFQ2cEphSDdnR2owdmI2U1dYZXJmTm16MVhFNXpqLXU0OXdvT29KcDkxeVRLb1lWSEJtSjZUQ08xcGhEZmw0eXBqOHoxZE9WRVVZcG82Vk5aaHlOc2lvNjVhQ1pSbw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxPUGNUdXRoYlVBY0dKSTNQZnFWbE4tWVI1SzJ1c2lXNU1JTEs0UnQ2RGVVT3lyLXdwX05xeVRrNDc4RU44WFhPcFRUNzloUlFQRV84bVJXVVh1X2dhdWRoRmw5U0UwOGhZ